{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And He did not continue.</b> They translate it: ״וְלָא פָּסִיק״ — 'and He did not cease.' (And because the nature of flesh and blood is that they cannot speak all their words in a single breath, but the nature of the Holy One, blessed be He, is not so — He did not cease, and since He did not cease, He did not add.) For His voice is strong and everlasting (Sanhedrin 17). Another interpretation: <b>and He did not continue</b> — He did not add to appear again in that public manner."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:06.974303541Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}